/-!
# Parameterized dependent calculus

Subject-level import inventory, including explicit instances and boundary
controls. Individual foundational modules do not import this inventory.
Language-specific adapters are intentionally excluded.

The shared grammar fixes Pi, Sigma, identity formation and reflexivity, with
declared constants and qualified root computation. It is a family of calculi,
not a claim to cover every dependent type theory. `HasType` is the raw judgment;
`FormationSensitive.Typing` retains the formation premises used by regularity.

`Instances` chooses concrete universe disciplines. `Examples` contains the
positive and negative witnesses; neither is a dependency of the generic laws.
`Computation` studies separately scoped effects, suspension references and
polarized values over the same dependent syntax. Its machine substrate lives
under `Mettapedia.Machines.BranchLocalNeed`.
-/
